Four maintained TypeScript modules add terminal-event handling for Google,
OpenAI Completions/Responses and Anthropic. Anthropic cancels its local SSE
reader on exit. The official Harness 0.1.7-alpha.1 adapter owns request
cancellation, consumer return and idle timeouts; no second transport owner
or Gemini URL/authentication rewrite is included. Runtime imports and proven
array bounds are adapted for this repository's strict compiler.

The fixed alpha.7 performance patch also removes repeated per-delta JSON
parsing in six providers, retaining final argument parsing. Bedrock, Mistral
and Pi Messages source modules are maintained for those official differences.

All other distribution files, including the full model catalog and unmodified
Responses entry point, come from the integrity-locked upstream npm archive.
ORIGIN.json records archive integrity, source recovery and original hashes,
and formal fork synchronization status. This is an unpublished candidate;
source synchronization is not complete-product installation validation.
Historical patches.json deltas must not be reapplied to this fork's builds.
